      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "(+)-Bicuculline, a close phthalideisoquinoline analogue, was directly measured in rat brain after systemic administration, demonstrating that this scaffold achieves BBB penetration and strongly supporting CNS access for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "α-Allocryptopine was detected in rat CSF after administration, providing direct evidence that related isoquinoline alkaloids cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "Tetrahydroberberine was detected in rat CSF, confirming CNS access for a structurally related alkaloid.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Schisandrin B showed a logPSFu,brain of -3.2 and reached 0.327 µg/g in mouse brain, demonstrating that lipophilic polycyclic natural products with similar physicochemical features penetrate brain tissue.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Nuciferine reached brain concentrations nearly equal to plasma in rats, demonstrating effective BBB crossing for a related aporphine alkaloid.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "Hernandezine achieved brain concentrations close to plasma Cmax after intravenous dosing in rats, supporting CNS access for this alkaloid class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Noscapine is predicted to have meaningful CNS access based on favorable passive BBB properties and consistent experimental evidence that structurally related phthalideisoquinoline and isoquinoline alkaloids cross the BBB in rodents, including direct brain and CSF detection.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental measurement of noscapine brain/CSF exposure is included in the provided evidence.",
    "Tumor/glioma-specific BBB permeability and potential efflux-transporter changes in the tumor microenvironment were not directly assessed.",
    "Most evidence comes from healthy rodents rather than brain-tumor models."
  ],
